      "claim": "L4 solubility and permeability records for beta-blocker analogs show aqueous solubility of at least 1 mg/mL (atenolol, propranolol, acebutolol, and a urea-containing aryloxypropanolamine analog) and propranolol Caco-2 permeability of about 3.4-3.7 x 10^-5 cm/s, supporting adequate intestinal absorption for this chemotype.",
      "card_ids": ["C54","C56","C59","C60","C61","C65","C57","C62"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall records show propranolol has high, symmetrical passive permeability with no P-gp/BCRP efflux, and atenolol has modest paracellular permeability; the celiprolol P-gp record indicates intestinal efflux for a close urea-containing beta-blocker analog but provides no F value and does not affirm F < 20%.",
