  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule; prediction relies on transfer from beta-blocker contexts.",
    "No query-specific permeability, solubility, or efflux measurement is available; L4/L5 records are for structurally related analogs.",
    "First-pass metabolism and systemic clearance of the urea-cyclohexyl aryloxypropanolamine are not directly measured.",
    "The celiprolol P-gp efflux record is mechanistic and does not quantify oral bioavailability for the query or for celiprolol itself."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L5 gut-wall/intestinal-metabolism records add no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F < 20%; propranolol no-efflux records support high passive permeability for the beta-blocker chemotype, and the celiprolol P-gp record is a mechanistic concern for a close analog but not a direct F outcome. Combined with transferable beta-blocker gold F values of 48-100% and favorable solubility/permeability for analogs, the prediction remains high."
}

